\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   It is fit for Christians
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 With fear and much attention
\par Keep vigil everyday,
\par And hold themselves with great care,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par It is fear and reverence
\par That leads to salvation.
\par If the upright suffered,
\par What fate shall sinner's be?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  And Satan hovers round,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Looking for us to swallow,
\par He so much ensnares us
\par In gloom to catch us thereby,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par This is a crazy world,
\par So caught up in his snares,
\par But this our mortal flesh,
\par Is our most worrying foe.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  We awfully transgress,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Because of sheer ignorance,
\par And it makes our spirits
\par Stand condemned before the Lord,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The acts of one sinner
\par  Is affective of all,
\par  Thus he that stands upright
\par Shall hold himself with care!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  The Lord God did declare:
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 I am a God so holy,
\par Hold thyselves pious too,
\par And thus be mine completely,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Sages of flesh exist,
\par But these I did not call
\par Christians who serve by mouth
\par Shall go to satan's hell.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When the just transgresses,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 His holiness becomes vain,
\par Someone knows my precepts,
\par Yet he cannot follow them,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When the servant who knows
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The precepts of his Lord
\par Fails to give them respect
\par He shall be punished much.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  The sins of Adam have,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 So many people destroyed,
\par And the wrath of the Lord,
\par Our dear Lord Christ did heareth.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your pact of baptism,
\par You do forget with ease.
\par But death cometh with speed,
\par Today or tomorrow.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Lord, when in spirit,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I remember all that I did,
\par It makes me shake with fear,
\par And gives me fright without bounds!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par For me, I trust you, Lord,
\par And yield unto Your care,
\par I plead for your mercy
\par Unto all in this world.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. In struggle and in stress,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Bid us tread with much caution;
\par And grant consolation
\par to make us able to bear
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Because of that great day,
\par Make us stay quite alert,
\par May we before Thee stand,
\par In perfect peace always.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

